WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
LARRY ARNN: The King is trying
to be all three branches.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.420
But the person
who can be trusted

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.470
to be all three branches is
actually named in the document.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.949
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.670
What is the general
rule, first paragraph?

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.140
SPEAKER 1: Well, it's the
fact that because of equality

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.740
and because all men are created
equal under the laws of nature,

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.865
they have the right to--

00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:33.320
LARRY ARNN: Under the laws
of nature and nature's God.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.000
Isn't that the first
authority cited in this?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.510
Right?

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.950
And Christian over here
mentions two other places

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.620
where God is mentioned
in the Declaration.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.390
What were they?

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.810
CHRISTIAN: They were where
it talked about endowed

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.570
with inalienable rights
by their creator, as well

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.730
as the end when we
pledge to each other

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.845
by the name of our
divine Providence.

00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:01.880
LARRY ARNN: Divine
Providence, creator, laws

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.897
of nature and of nature's God.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:04.939
Can you think of another?

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.990
No.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:22.900
So the answer is, supreme judge
of the world toward the end.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:25.590
So what branch of
government would

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:32.350
be the maker of the laws of
nature and of nature's God?

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.530
SPEAKER 2: Legislator?

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.620
LARRY ARNN: Lawmaker.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.610
God is a lawmaker, right?

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:44.970
What branch of government would
be supreme judge of the world?

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.350
ALL: Judiciary.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.190
LARRY ARNN: Yeah.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:52.180
What branch of government
would be divine Providence?

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.230
ALL: Executive.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:55.210
LARRY ARNN: I'll be darned.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.970
And the creator would be
like a founder, right?

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.050
Like a Constitution maker.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.900
Now, it's very
interesting that God

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:07.660
appears in these guises
and these images.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.110
The branches of government,
one of the charges

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.480
in the middle of the
Declaration of Independence

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.540
is that the king, who's
the executive branch,

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.890
has interfered with the
legislature and the judges.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.020
He suspended the legislature.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.660
He has removed judges.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.510
He has interfered with
the trial by jury.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:34.040
The king is trying to
be all three branches.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.100
But the person
who can be trusted

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.560
to be all three
branches is actually

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.500
named in the document--

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.190
only God, right?

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.880
It's very plain, isn't it?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.340
Now, what do you mean
by a law of nature?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.625
STEVE: Kind of rules that govern
how things should operate.

00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:58.740
LARRY ARNN: You can
make it specific.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.490
That's good.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.600
That's very good, Steve.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.520
And you can make it
specific this way too,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:09.770
because if we say that a thing
has a way of growing, well,

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.980
under what conditions
does it grow well?

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.380
Plants need sun and
Sequoia trees need space.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:24.260
Whatever makes it thrive,
that's the law governing it.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.850
And the laws of nature
and of nature's God,

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.310
they're referring there
to this God that appears

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.380
three other times, right?

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.680
The one responsible for
the order of all things,

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:42.050
and also, the great
majority of them, the one

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:48.230
to whom they pray and expect
them to protect the revolution

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:50.390
that they're waging.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.630
Not all of them thought
that God was so.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.700
But many did, and
we're going to learn

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.060
as we go that it was a
specific purpose of the United

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.000
States of America to
be the first country

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:07.160
to make a complete, and full,
and happy home for people who

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.130
thought both ways about that.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.070
Because their idea
was, those who

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.770
were Christians, who were
the great majority of them,

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.050
their idea was
you're never going

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:21.019
to get to heaven because
somebody passed a law saying

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:23.060
you had to do something.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.510
SPEAKER 3: Thank
you for watching.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.480
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlights series

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.390
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.560
online courses.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.500
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

